WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.667 --> 00:00:02.735
-Our next guest is
an Academy Award-nominated

00:00:02.735 --> 00:00:04.236
and Emmy Award-winning producer

00:00:04.236 --> 00:00:06.372
His latest work,
"The Exorcist: Believer,"

00:00:06.372 --> 00:00:09.808
is out now, and his other movie,
"Friday Nights at Freddy's,"

00:00:09.808 --> 00:00:12.712
comes to theaters and streaming
on Peacock October 27th.

00:00:12.712 --> 00:00:13.879
Let's take a look.

00:00:13.879 --> 00:00:14.948
[Buzzes]

00:00:14.948 --> 00:00:16.282
-You must be
the new security guard.

00:00:16.282 --> 00:00:19.718
-Back in the '80s,
some kids went missing.

00:00:19.718 --> 00:00:21.754
That's why the place shut down.

00:00:21.754 --> 00:00:23.255
What is she doing here?

00:00:23.255 --> 00:00:25.491
-I couldn't find a sitter.

00:00:25.491 --> 00:00:26.893
What are you so afraid of?

00:00:26.893 --> 00:00:28.628
-Them.

00:00:30.063 --> 00:00:31.130
[ Screams ]

00:00:31.130 --> 00:00:32.565
-Please welcome back
to the show,

00:00:32.565 --> 00:00:34.767
our good friend Jason Blum,
everybody!

00:00:34.767 --> 00:00:37.437
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:37.437 --> 00:00:49.515 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:49.515 --> 00:00:52.351
Welcome back, my friend.

00:00:52.351 --> 00:00:54.086
-Thrilled to be here.

00:00:54.086 --> 00:00:56.355
"Five Nights at Freddy's"
-Five. What did I say?

00:00:56.355 --> 00:00:58.324
-"Friday Nights at Freddy's."
-I said Friday.

00:00:58.324 --> 00:00:59.559
It's "Five Nights at Freddy's."

00:00:59.559 --> 00:01:01.227
-Everyone says
"Friday Nights at Freddy's."

00:01:01.227 --> 00:01:02.395
-Why do we get it wrong?

00:01:02.395 --> 00:01:03.696
-"Five Nights at Freddy's."
I don't know.

00:01:03.696 --> 00:01:05.765
The sequel is going to be
"Friday Nights at Freddy's."

00:01:05.765 --> 00:01:07.366
The guy who created
it just had a heart attack.

00:01:07.366 --> 00:01:09.302
-Oh, my God.
"Five Nights at Freddy's."

00:01:09.302 --> 00:01:10.336
Alright. That's very --

00:01:10.336 --> 00:01:12.105
And this
is based on a video game.

00:01:12.105 --> 00:01:15.874
-This is based on a video game
and very, very complicated lore,

00:01:15.874 --> 00:01:18.778
and I've been working on it --
I've worked on this movie

00:01:18.778 --> 00:01:20.980
longer than anything else
we've ever done.

00:01:20.980 --> 00:01:23.283
I've worked on it,
it's been 8 or 9 years

00:01:23.283 --> 00:01:26.151
since I first met Scott Cawthon,
who created this,

00:01:26.151 --> 00:01:29.154
and he's
a wildly creative genius

00:01:29.154 --> 00:01:30.657
and he lives in Texas.

00:01:30.657 --> 00:01:35.528
And it was very, very important
to him that it be just so.

00:01:35.528 --> 00:01:38.631
We went through
8 directors and 15 scripts,

00:01:38.631 --> 00:01:42.034
and I'm very, very proud
we finally got the movie.

00:01:42.034 --> 00:01:43.803
-And then I'm out here
just getting the title wrong.

00:01:43.803 --> 00:01:48.307
-Yeah, and then you destroyed it
in a heartbeat.

00:01:48.307 --> 00:01:49.442
-12 years of your life!

00:01:49.442 --> 00:01:50.977
-12 years of my life, ruined.

00:01:50.977 --> 00:01:52.945
Now, we did something
interesting on the movie.

00:01:52.945 --> 00:01:57.149
Usually, when Hollywood
attacks a video game or a book,

00:01:57.149 --> 00:01:58.784
they always say, like,
"We're going to make it

00:01:58.784 --> 00:02:00.954
for the fans and we're going to
make it for everybody else."

00:02:00.954 --> 00:02:02.856
I probably shouldn't be saying
this on national television,

00:02:02.856 --> 00:02:04.491
but I'm just going to go for it.
-That's alright. It's on late.

00:02:04.491 --> 00:02:06.759
-Yeah, yeah. True, true. Not
that many people. Okay, fine.

00:02:06.759 --> 00:02:10.596
So what what
what Scott wanted to do,

00:02:10.596 --> 00:02:12.331
which is an experiment,
we'll see how it works.

00:02:12.331 --> 00:02:14.633
I thought it was a very
cool idea, so we said yes,

00:02:14.633 --> 00:02:18.471
is we are only
making this for fans

00:02:18.471 --> 00:02:19.805
of "Five Nights at Freddy's."

00:02:19.805 --> 00:02:21.707
If other people want to see it,
that's fine with us.

00:02:21.707 --> 00:02:22.942
We're very happy.

00:02:22.942 --> 00:02:25.044
But we're not trying
to expand the audience.

00:02:25.044 --> 00:02:28.648
We're trying to keep
the fans thrilled.

00:02:28.648 --> 00:02:30.816
And of course,
we won't make everyone happy,

00:02:30.816 --> 00:02:32.084
but that's what we did

00:02:32.084 --> 00:02:34.653
setting out to make the movie,
which is unusual.

00:02:34.653 --> 00:02:36.688
And as I said,
the PR team probably now

00:02:36.688 --> 00:02:39.225
is going to come assassinate me,
but that's what we did.

00:02:39.225 --> 00:02:42.095
-And do you feel that there is
a groundswell of excitement

00:02:42.095 --> 00:02:43.929
from the fans, knowing
that this is the approach?

00:02:43.929 --> 00:02:46.332
-Yes, the movie is right now --

00:02:46.332 --> 00:02:48.701
I have a little grin on my face,

00:02:48.701 --> 00:02:50.536
because the movie
is looking like --

00:02:50.536 --> 00:02:52.839
you never know with these
things, as I recently learned,

00:02:52.839 --> 00:02:56.642
but it's looking like it
is going to way overperform

00:02:56.642 --> 00:02:58.877
what anyone, including myself,
thought it would do.

00:02:58.877 --> 00:03:00.313
So knock on wood, that happens.

00:03:00.313 --> 00:03:02.614
-Knock on wood. Very exciting.
-So far, so good.

00:03:02.614 --> 00:03:04.851
-You are
a horror movie producer.

00:03:04.851 --> 00:03:07.119
This should come as no surprise,
you love Halloween.

00:03:07.119 --> 00:03:08.488
-I'm a Halloween expert.

00:03:08.488 --> 00:03:10.456
-Favorite holiday?
-I'm like Santa for Halloween.

00:03:10.456 --> 00:03:11.624
-You are like Santa
for Halloween.

00:03:11.624 --> 00:03:12.892
Yes, I've been
at Halloween parties.

00:03:12.892 --> 00:03:15.360
You show up, never,
not once without a costume.

00:03:15.360 --> 00:03:16.762
-I don't mess around.

00:03:16.762 --> 00:03:19.131
-But you also have access
to very good makeup people,

00:03:19.131 --> 00:03:20.566
very good costumes.

00:03:20.566 --> 00:03:22.035
-No, it's true, I cheat a bit.
-You cheat a bit.

00:03:22.035 --> 00:03:24.236
Like, for example,
you and your wife,

00:03:24.236 --> 00:03:25.538
your beautiful wife Lauren --

00:03:25.538 --> 00:03:28.574
decided to be Stormy Daniels
and Michael Avenatti

00:03:28.574 --> 00:03:30.142
a few years ago.
-Yes, we did.

00:03:30.142 --> 00:03:31.410
-But you went
a different way with it.

00:03:31.410 --> 00:03:33.545
-Yes, we did.
We flipped genders.

00:03:33.545 --> 00:03:34.714
-You flipped genders.

00:03:35.949 --> 00:03:38.551
-Not bad.

00:03:38.551 --> 00:03:39.952
-Come on!

00:03:39.952 --> 00:03:41.187
-That's you.
-That was incredible.

00:03:41.187 --> 00:03:42.421
-That's incredible.

00:03:42.421 --> 00:03:43.789
-People look at -- when
I show that to people,

00:03:43.789 --> 00:03:45.425
they really, they look.

00:03:45.425 --> 00:03:46.725
It takes like, four seconds

00:03:46.725 --> 00:03:48.294
to understand
what's actually happening.

00:03:48.294 --> 00:03:50.730
-Yeah.
-But this is actually me,

00:03:50.730 --> 00:03:52.532
and this is actually my wife.

00:03:52.532 --> 00:03:54.466
-And how uncomfortable
was that evening?

00:03:54.466 --> 00:03:55.401
-It was --

00:03:55.401 --> 00:03:57.636
It was actually physically,

00:03:57.636 --> 00:03:59.104
profoundly uncomfortable
because I had

00:03:59.104 --> 00:04:00.372
10 pounds of prosthetics on me.

00:04:00.372 --> 00:04:01.574
Is that what you mean?
-Yeah.

00:04:01.574 --> 00:04:03.042
-It was very and very
uncomfortable and sweaty,

00:04:03.042 --> 00:04:05.177
and I feel terrible for women
in these clothes

00:04:05.177 --> 00:04:06.511
that they have to wear, it's
horrible, and in high heels.

00:04:06.511 --> 00:04:08.314
-Did not stop you guys

00:04:08.314 --> 00:04:09.515
from doing Jared and Ivanka,
though.

00:04:09.515 --> 00:04:10.449
-Jared and Ivanka.

00:04:10.449 --> 00:04:12.852
-Yeah.
-That was a great one.

00:04:12.852 --> 00:04:14.786
Remember when Jared put on
that crazy vest,

00:04:14.786 --> 00:04:17.422
you thought he was fighting
the war in Afghanistan?

00:04:17.422 --> 00:04:18.991
This was great.

00:04:18.991 --> 00:04:20.592
-You produced, "M3GAN,"
a fantastic film.

00:04:20.592 --> 00:04:21.694
-Yes, a great film.
-And you decided --

00:04:21.694 --> 00:04:22.928
[ Applause ]

00:04:22.928 --> 00:04:25.598
-There we go. Give it up.
-Thank you. Thank you.

00:04:25.598 --> 00:04:28.034
-You -- The red carpet had
multiple M3GANs.

00:04:28.034 --> 00:04:30.403
I don't want to give it away
for the audience.

00:04:30.403 --> 00:04:31.970
-Yes, go ahead.
-There's five M3GANS

00:04:31.970 --> 00:04:33.172
in this photo.
-Yes, yes.

00:04:33.172 --> 00:04:35.708
-Jason is one of the M3GANs.
-This is tricky.

00:04:38.177 --> 00:04:40.747
[ Laughter ]

00:04:40.747 --> 00:04:42.447
-This might be best of all.

00:04:42.447 --> 00:04:43.949
You did
Wicked Witch of the West.

00:04:43.949 --> 00:04:46.419
And I mean, this is fantastic.

00:04:46.419 --> 00:04:47.887
Look at you.
-You know.

00:04:47.887 --> 00:04:49.755
-And then finally,
you let Lauren

00:04:49.755 --> 00:04:51.657
be appropriate as Dorothy there.
-Yeah, yeah.

00:04:51.657 --> 00:04:53.726
I look like a witch
in real life, so it worked.

00:04:53.726 --> 00:04:57.229
-Now, you had a very
interesting producer problem

00:04:57.229 --> 00:04:59.231
that you ran into,
because I don't think people

00:04:59.231 --> 00:05:02.201
appreciate how important a date
is to when a movie comes out.

00:05:02.201 --> 00:05:04.703
So you have this movie,
"The Exorcist,"

00:05:04.703 --> 00:05:06.372
you have a date picked out,
a date you're excited about.

00:05:06.372 --> 00:05:07.640
-Yes.

00:05:07.640 --> 00:05:10.609
-And usually, you know
which movies are coming.

00:05:10.609 --> 00:05:12.178
Movies never come
out of nowhere.

00:05:12.178 --> 00:05:13.312
-No.
-And then one did.

00:05:13.312 --> 00:05:14.613
-And then one did.

00:05:14.613 --> 00:05:17.382
-This was a terrible tragedy
in the Blum household.

00:05:17.382 --> 00:05:21.553
Friday the 13th in October
is the single greatest day

00:05:21.553 --> 00:05:23.522
to release a horror movie,
and it only comes around

00:05:23.522 --> 00:05:25.258
once every seven years
because there aren't that many.

00:05:25.258 --> 00:05:26.959
Friday the 13ths in October,

00:05:26.959 --> 00:05:28.761
they're just the once
every seven years.

00:05:28.761 --> 00:05:33.032
So we date "The Exorcist" on the
greatest date for horror movies,

00:05:33.032 --> 00:05:35.768
that comes around
very infrequently

00:05:35.768 --> 00:05:40.406
and about eight weeks ago,

00:05:40.406 --> 00:05:44.076
which is the last possible
minute you can change a date,

00:05:44.076 --> 00:05:48.381
Taylor Swift drops on my date.

00:05:48.381 --> 00:05:51.583
I try and save the day
by "ExorSwift."

00:05:51.583 --> 00:05:54.387
I try and make --
I'm hoping, praying,

00:05:54.387 --> 00:05:55.721
that this is going to work.

00:05:55.721 --> 00:05:58.223
-When you say you tried to make
"ExorSwift" a thing,

00:05:58.223 --> 00:05:59.825
here's his efforts, by the way.

00:05:59.825 --> 00:06:00.927
-"Exorswift."

00:06:00.927 --> 00:06:02.828
Yeah, well,
I didn't try that hard.

00:06:02.828 --> 00:06:06.833
I didn't try that hard.
I tried, I tried.

00:06:06.833 --> 00:06:07.866
Three hours,

00:06:07.866 --> 00:06:10.235
three hours after
after I tweet that,

00:06:10.235 --> 00:06:12.138
the head of the marketing,

00:06:12.138 --> 00:06:14.540
amazing partner Michael Moses,
calls me and says,

00:06:14.540 --> 00:06:16.775
"It's not working.
We got to move the movie."

00:06:16.775 --> 00:06:18.243
-And so, and then,
this is the follow-up tweet

00:06:18.243 --> 00:06:19.378
just a little bit --

00:06:19.378 --> 00:06:20.412
"Look what you made me do.

00:06:20.412 --> 00:06:22.114
"The Exorcist: Believer"
moves to 10/6.

00:06:22.114 --> 00:06:23.148
#TaylorWins.

00:06:23.148 --> 00:06:25.584
-Taylor wins.

00:06:25.584 --> 00:06:26.986
Yeah, I was trying
to be a nice guy,

00:06:26.986 --> 00:06:28.754
because Taylor Swift is
my daughter's favorite singer,

00:06:28.754 --> 00:06:34.193
but underneath this tweet there
was rage, rage, rage.

00:06:34.193 --> 00:06:36.161
-And it affected
the whole Blum household,

00:06:36.161 --> 00:06:37.729
because your wife, Lauren Blum,

00:06:37.729 --> 00:06:39.365
who's a fantastic
screenwriter --

00:06:39.365 --> 00:06:40.466
-Incredible.

00:06:40.466 --> 00:06:42.335
-Her and her partner,
Rebecca Angelo,

00:06:42.335 --> 00:06:45.204
wrote a fantastic film
called "Dumb Money."

00:06:45.204 --> 00:06:46.806
-Yes, exactly.
-"Dumb Money."

00:06:46.806 --> 00:06:48.608
[ Applause ]

00:06:48.608 --> 00:06:50.943
And "Dumb Money" is up
against a problem

00:06:50.943 --> 00:06:52.711
a lot of these
smaller movies are having.

00:06:52.711 --> 00:06:55.514
SAG actors cannot promote
the film.

00:06:55.514 --> 00:06:57.383
But she had
to move her date as well.

00:06:57.383 --> 00:06:59.518
-Well, so what happened is,

00:06:59.518 --> 00:07:01.220
we had to move the movie back,

00:07:01.220 --> 00:07:04.790
and it just so happened that
"Dumb Money" was on that date.

00:07:04.790 --> 00:07:09.228
So not only did Taylor Swift
destroy my Friday the 13th

00:07:09.228 --> 00:07:13.299
and kill this
incredible date I had,

00:07:13.299 --> 00:07:16.001
she almost caused me
to get divorced.

00:07:16.001 --> 00:07:17.303
-Because you moved
back to 10/6...

00:07:17.303 --> 00:07:19.471
-We put on "Dumb Money,"
and my wife said

00:07:19.471 --> 00:07:20.940
"You can move anywhere else,
but not there."

00:07:20.940 --> 00:07:23.208
I said,
"There's nowhere else to go."

00:07:23.208 --> 00:07:28.114
And it was a very tense
24 hours, until my poor wife

00:07:28.114 --> 00:07:31.884
had to move her
spectacular movie earlier.

00:07:31.884 --> 00:07:33.585
But it's very hard,
these movies,

00:07:33.585 --> 00:07:35.855
especially in today's
environment, it's very fragile

00:07:35.855 --> 00:07:38.257
and it's very delicate
and moving release dates

00:07:38.257 --> 00:07:40.192
is not something you want to do.

00:07:40.192 --> 00:07:41.526
So what can I do?

00:07:41.526 --> 00:07:44.563
My daughter loves Taylor Swift,
so I feel bad, you know?

00:07:44.563 --> 00:07:47.065
And everyone loves Taylor Swift,
so if I said anything bad --

00:07:47.065 --> 00:07:48.767
-Taylor Swift
is going to be fine.

00:07:48.767 --> 00:07:51.169
-Taylor Swift
loves Taylor Swift.

00:07:51.169 --> 00:07:52.738
-I love Taylor Swift!

00:07:52.738 --> 00:07:54.507
-I can't get Taylor Swift?

00:07:54.507 --> 00:07:56.542
I can't affect her by talking
about her on this show?

00:07:56.542 --> 00:07:58.744
-No, I think her movie
is going to do just fine.

00:07:58.744 --> 00:08:01.347
-No, that's the problem.
It's going to do amazing.

00:08:01.347 --> 00:08:04.316
It's going to do amazing,
and we had to move.

00:08:04.316 --> 00:08:05.751
We had to move all our movies.
We almost got divorced.

00:08:05.751 --> 00:08:07.853
-Did you think about maybe in
the middle of "The Exorcist"

00:08:07.853 --> 00:08:10.823
just adding a scene
of like, Taylor Swift singing?

00:08:10.823 --> 00:08:11.957
-I did. Actually, I did.

00:08:11.957 --> 00:08:13.492
I said,
"We could either move the date,

00:08:13.492 --> 00:08:17.029
we could just add some of
her footage into the movie."

00:08:17.029 --> 00:08:18.965
-You got one of your dreams
coming true.

00:08:18.965 --> 00:08:20.565
You are going to be
a judge on Shark Tank.

00:08:20.565 --> 00:08:23.102
-Oh, yes. This is very
exciting to talk about.

00:08:23.102 --> 00:08:25.971
[ Applause ]
-Yeah, tell me more.

00:08:25.971 --> 00:08:28.140
-I get asked by people.

00:08:28.140 --> 00:08:31.176
This is actually, I'll connect
to your show for a sec.

00:08:31.176 --> 00:08:32.311
I get asked by people,

00:08:32.311 --> 00:08:33.879
"So did they ask you
to do 'Shark Tank'?"

00:08:33.879 --> 00:08:35.748
I don't know about all these
other successful people.

00:08:35.748 --> 00:08:36.949
I've never been asked to do --

00:08:36.949 --> 00:08:39.084
I begged to be on "Shark Tank"
for 20 years,

00:08:39.084 --> 00:08:41.286
just like I begged to be
on your show for 20 years.

00:08:41.286 --> 00:08:42.554
I mean, very similar.
-Yeah.

00:08:42.554 --> 00:08:45.458
-Anyway, they finally said yes,
and it was great.

00:08:45.458 --> 00:08:48.427
And then of course, I get on
"Shark Tank" and I'm doing...

00:08:48.427 --> 00:08:51.530
Now everyone says, "So what are
you selling on 'Shark Tank'?"

00:08:51.530 --> 00:08:53.466
I'm like, "I'm a Shark,
for God's sake!

00:08:53.466 --> 00:08:55.801
I'm not [bleep].
I'm not selling."

00:08:55.801 --> 00:08:59.604
They think I'm selling
Blumhouse on "Shark Tank."

00:08:59.604 --> 00:09:03.209
For $1 million,
you can have 10% of Blumhouse.

00:09:03.209 --> 00:09:05.645
So anyway, I was a shark
on "Shark Tank."

00:09:05.645 --> 00:09:07.747
I did it, they taped
two episodes for the day.

00:09:07.747 --> 00:09:10.116
You go at 8:00 and you leave
at 8:00 at night or whatever.

00:09:10.116 --> 00:09:12.918
It was really fun.
It was really exciting.

00:09:12.918 --> 00:09:16.254
And I had a great day. And it
airs -- it airs very soon.

00:09:16.254 --> 00:09:18.925
I should know the date when I'm
supposed to be plugging it --

00:09:18.925 --> 00:09:20.292
-All you know are
the dates of your movies.

00:09:20.292 --> 00:09:22.828
-All I know is the dates
of Taylor Swift, "ExorSwift."

00:09:22.828 --> 00:09:24.796
-#ExorSwift.

00:09:24.796 --> 00:09:26.232
-It comes out at the end
of this month.

00:09:26.232 --> 00:09:28.734
-And were there,
just as a little teaser,

00:09:28.734 --> 00:09:30.169
were there anything
you were impressed by?

00:09:30.169 --> 00:09:31.971
-There were some things I was --

00:09:31.971 --> 00:09:34.006
I've been instructed very --

00:09:34.006 --> 00:09:35.574
You can't say
if you invested or not,

00:09:35.574 --> 00:09:38.076
so you'll have to watch
the show to find out.

00:09:38.076 --> 00:09:40.512
But there were several things
I was very interested in

00:09:40.512 --> 00:09:42.047
and it was
it was actually very fun

